  "id": "isometric-control",
  "term": "isometric control",
  "definition": "Isometric control, in this learning context, means regulating force output to match and hold a set target level, such as 40% of maximum force, during an isometric force task. It can also refer to how accurately that force is maintained and how well performance adapts when the target is unexpectedly changed.",
